{"id":"000VMC","title":"The Long Way Home","author":"Kafkapharnaum","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-20T07:41:27+00:00","posted":"Heute, 06:34 Uhr","rules":"A Coordinate Arrow Chaos Construction clearly inspired by this mighty one, but which applies instead a more common use of CC arrows to the tips of the Coordinate Arrows for the purpose of region building.\n\nBig thanks once again to chrisj50 for testing!\n\nClick on the puzzle to play\n\nRULES\n\nCHAOS CONSTRUCTION\n\n— Divide the grid into nine regions, each made of nine orthogonally connected cells, such that each row, column and nine cell region contains the digits 1 to 9 exactly once each.\n\nCOORDINATE ARROWS\n\n— Digits on an arrow spell out the coordinates for a digit that is their sum (the target cell): the row number is written on the tail of the arrow, and the column number is written on the arrow tip. Eg, an arrow reading -1-4-> would indicate a 5 in the target cell r1c4.\n\n— In addition, a digit *n* on the tip of an arrow indicates that *n* cells away in that direction lies a cell (the 'companion cell') belonging to the same region as this arrow's target cell, which companion cell may or may not be the target cell itself.\n\n— No two arrows can spell out the same coordinates, but two arrows can lead to the same companion cell, provided they don't contain the same coordinates.\n\n— All arrows are to be considered individually with regards to the above rules, even when they share a cell with another arrow.","solutionCode":"From top to bottom, the digit in column 7, with a - (dash/hyphen) to indicate region borders (grid edges can be ignored).","tags":["Sudoku","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/t1l7pgagle","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/t1l7pgagle","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-20T07:41:27+00:00"}